{"body":"## Background\n\nThe current iroh configuration in `crates/radicle-artifact-node/src/iroh.rs` uses `.address_lookup(DnsAddressLookup::builder(self.dns_endpoint_origin))` for DNS resolution, which performs unencrypted UDP DNS.\n\nWe'd like to move towards encrypted endpoint discovery.\n\n## Options\n\nThere are a couple of ways to do this:\n\n- Configure the `PkarrResolver` only, instead of using `DnsAddressLookup`. This uses HTTPS to the pkarr server.\n- Configure a `DnsResolver` with only HTTPS nameservers. See `Endpoint::builder().dns_resolver()` and `DnsResolver::builder().with_nameservers`.\n\n## Maintainer insight\n\nThe iroh maintainer shared the following:\n\n- A DoH-only `DnsResolver` applies to *all* DNS resolution in iroh. Apart from endpoint address lookup, this includes looking up relay URL domains and pkarr server addresses (for publishing).\n- DNS lookup with a DoH resolver goes to the configured DoH server, which then forwards the query to the upstream DNS server. It can be faster if the server is close to you and has records cached. The caching can also be unwanted if you are dealing with frequently changing information. The `PkarrResolver` goes directly to the origin server, so it always gets the latest info, at potentially higher latency.\n\n## Proposed direction\n\nLean towards using `PkarrResolver` so that endpoints are resolved in an encrypted fashion, while the relay and pkarr endpoints are resolved using system DNS.","type":"comment"}